@page "/desktop-sales"
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using ShopInventory.Web.Services
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Cashier")]
@inject IDesktopIntegrationService DesktopService
@inject IMasterDataCacheService MasterDataCache
@inject IReportExportService ExportService
@inject INotificationHubService HubService
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@inject ISnackbar Snackbar
@inject IAuditService AuditService
@implements IDisposable
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Desktop Sales - Shop Inventory</PageTitle>

@* Built from `Desktop Sales.dc.html` in the "Nocturne Dark Ops Redesign" design
   project. Styles live in wwwroot/css/operations.css (linked from App.razor),
   shared with the other five operational pages — see that file's header for why
   an imported design joined the derived sheet rather than taking one of its
   own. `ops` is the scope; `ops-ds` is this page's own half of it. The 542-line
   inline <style> block is gone.

   **The design's row selection is built now, against a different verb.** It
   drew a checkbox per row and a "Consolidate 4" button — consolidating a chosen
   subset — and that stayed unbuilt while `TriggerConsolidationAsync()` took no
   arguments: checkboxes that did not decide what gets consolidated would have
   been a lie about what the button does.

   `POST sales/post-batch` is the selective endpoint that was missing, so the
   column exists and carries the verb the API actually offers. **Posting is not
   consolidating**, and the two must not be confused by anyone reading this
   page: consolidating is the end-of-day run that folds a day's legacy-desktop
   sales into one invoice per customer, while posting sends the chosen till, van
   and vending sales to SAP as one invoice each — the same thing the background
   pass does every minute, asked for now. So the hero keeps both buttons, and
   only a sale the API says is postable gets a checkbox.

   **The design's second revision** brought the rest of what is here: the lane
   strip above the counts rather than below them, the counts as a four-up grid,
   a filter row on a wash carrying the count it is the answer to, a hover cue on
   a row that opens a drawer, and a drawer that states the document — a headline
   amount, the fiscal block the device signed, and a trail.

   Its remaining per-sale actions are still not drawn, and for the original
   reason. "Consolidate now" in a drawer about one invoice is not Post to SAP:
   posting sends this sale to SAP as its own invoice, consolidating closes the
   whole day. There is still no endpoint that excludes a sale from the close,
   and no receipt PDF is kept for a desktop sale.

   Four places where the design assumed data this page does not have:

   - Its status lanes come from the end-of-day report's consolidation counts
     rather than an invented per-device lifecycle, and its per-site value bars
     became per-customer, because `BusinessPartnerSummaries` is the breakdown
     the report returns.
   - Its drawer prints a raised time and a fiscalized time. A desktop sale
     carries `CreatedAt` and nothing else, so one stamp is stated once.
   - Its trail ends at "Posted to ledger" with a journal number. There is no
     ledger posting time on this row. There is a SAP document number, by two
     routes that write different columns — see `trail` — and that is what the
     last step states.
   - Its "fiscal signature" is a line of text. The signature is a URL, so it is
     drawn as the scannable thing it is: the QR panel is where that part of the
     design landed, with the verification code and the same URL as a link beside
     it. *@

<div class="ops ops-ds">

    <div class="ops-hero">
        <div class="ops-hero-text">
            <div class="ops-ds-kicker-row">
                <span class="ops-kicker">Offline fiscalization</span>
                <span class="ops-ds-kicker-rule"></span>
                @* The dot animates only while the hub is up. A still dot is the
                   disconnected state, not an animation that failed to start. *@
                <span class="ops-ds-live">
                    <span class="ops-ds-live-dot @(HubService.IsConnected ? "" : "is-off")"></span>
                    @(HubService.IsConnected ? "Live" : "Offline")
                </span>
            </div>
            <h1>Desktop Sales</h1>
            <p>
                Invoices raised in the desktop apps and fiscalized on the local device.
                They stay here until the day is consolidated into the back office.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ops-ds-hero-side">
            <div class="ops-ds-poll">
                <div class="ops-ds-poll-now">
                    @(lastPolledAt.HasValue ? $"Polled {lastPolledAt:HH:mm:ss}" : "Not polled yet")
                </div>
                <div class="ops-ds-poll-then">
                    @(report != null ? $"Report generated {report.GeneratedAt.AddHours(2):dd MMM, HH:mm}" : "No report yet")
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ops-hero-actions">
                @* Only while something is selected. A permanently visible "Post 0 to SAP" would
                   invite the press that does nothing, and the count is the whole point of the
                   button: it states what is about to reach SAP before it does. *@
                @if (selected.Count > 0)
                {
                    <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-primary" @onclick="OpenBulkPost"
                            disabled="@(isPosting || isLoading)">
                        @if (isPosting)
                        {
                            <span class="ops-spin"></span>
                            <span>Posting&hellip;</span>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <i class="ph ph-cloud-arrow-up" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span>Post @selected.Count to SAP</span>
                        }
                    </button>
                }
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-primary" @onclick="OpenConsolidate"
                        disabled="@(isConsolidating || isLoading)">
                    @if (isConsolidating)
                    {
                        <span class="ops-spin"></span>
                        <span>Consolidating&hellip;</span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <i class="ph ph-paper-plane-tilt" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>Consolidate day</span>
                    }
                </button>
                @* The same sales, summed: by payment method, day, hour, shop and item. *@
                <a class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" href="/reports/desktop-sales">
                    <i class="ph ph-chart-pie-slice" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span>Sales analysis</span>
                </a>
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" @onclick="ExportToExcel"
                        disabled="@(isExporting || sales.Count == 0)">
                    @if (isExporting)
                    {
                        <span class="ops-spin"></span>
                        <span>Exporting&hellip;</span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <i class="ph ph-file-xls" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>Export</span>
                    }
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="ops-icon-btn" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh"
                        @onclick="RefreshData" disabled="@isLoading">
                    @if (isLoading)
                    {
                        <span class="ops-spin"></span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <i class="ph ph-arrows-clockwise" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    }
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ops-rule-fade"></div>

    @if (report != null)
    {
        <div class="ops-ds-summary">
            @* The day, divided. The strip states the split before the four
               numbers do, so the shape of the day is readable before a single
               figure is; each lane and its share of the strip read the same
               family, so a lane cannot be one colour and its bar another. *@
            <div class="ops-ds-card">
                <div class="ops-ds-card-head">
                    <span class="ops-ds-card-label">@dayLabel</span>
                    <span class="ops-ds-card-tally">
                        <b>@report.TotalSalesCount</b>
                        <span>fiscalized</span>
                    </span>
                </div>

                @if (laneTotal > 0)
                {
                    <div class="ops-ds-strip">
                        @foreach (var lane in lanes.Where(l => l.Count > 0))
                        {
                            <div class="ops-ds-strip-seg @lane.Family"
                                 style="width:@Percent(lane.Count, laneTotal)"></div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }

                <div class="ops-ds-lanes">
                    @foreach (var lane in lanes)
                    {
                        <div class="ops-ds-lane @lane.Family">
                            <div class="ops-ds-lane-num">@lane.Count</div>
                            <div class="ops-ds-lane-name">@lane.Name</div>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>

                @* Net, not the gross the day totals to: the design states the
                   three amounts side by side, and Net beside VAT that adds up
                   to something else would be read as an arithmetic error.
                   `TotalSalesAmount` is subtotal + VAT — see
                   CreateDesktopSaleHandler — so the subtraction is exact. *@
                <div class="ops-ds-aside ops-ds-aside-ruled">
                    <span>Net <b>@Money(report.TotalSalesAmount - report.TotalVatAmount)</b></span>
                    <span>VAT <b>@Money(report.TotalVatAmount)</b></span>
                    <span>Paid <b>@Money(report.TotalAmountPaid)</b></span>
                </div>
            </div>

            @* The headline is what has *not* reached the back office yet, not
               the day's total — that number is the one the Consolidate button
               acts on, and the day's total is stated beside the lanes. *@
            <div class="ops-ds-card">
                <div class="ops-ds-card-head">
                    <i class="ph ph-hard-drives" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="ops-ds-card-label">Value on the device</span>
                </div>

                <div class="ops-ds-value">
                    <b>@Money(awaitingValue)</b>
                </div>
                <div class="ops-ds-aside">
                    <span>not yet in the back office · @report.UnpostedInvoiceCount awaiting close</span>
                </div>

                @if (topPartners.Count > 0)
                {
                    <div class="ops-ds-split"></div>
                    <div class="ops-ds-breakdown">
                        <div class="ops-ds-card-label">Largest customers</div>
                        @foreach (var partner in topPartners)
                        {
                            <div class="ops-ds-break-row">
                                <span class="ops-ds-break-code" title="@(partner.CardName ?? partner.CardCode)">
                                    @partner.CardCode
                                </span>
                                <span class="ops-ds-break-track">
                                    <span class="ops-ds-break-fill"
                                          style="width:@Percent(partner.TotalAmount, topPartnerMax)"></span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="ops-ds-break-val">@Money(partner.TotalAmount)</span>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }

    @if (notice != null)
    {
        <div class="ops-msg @noticeFamily" role="alert">
            <i class="ph @noticeIcon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <div class="ops-msg-body">@notice</div>
            <button type="button" class="ops-msg-x" aria-label="Dismiss" @onclick="() => notice = null">
                <i class="ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
    }

    <div class="ops-ds-filters">
        <div class="ops-field">
            <label class="ops-label" for="ds-warehouse">Warehouse</label>
            <NocturneSelect Id="ds-warehouse" Class="nsel-block" Options="WarehouseFilterOptions"
                            @bind-Value="filterWarehouse" OnChanged="ApplyFilters"
                            Caption="Filter by warehouse" AriaLabel="Filter by warehouse"
                            Placeholder="All warehouses" />
        </div>

        <div class="ops-field ops-field-wide">
            <label class="ops-label" for="ds-customer">Customer</label>
            @* The API filters on card code alone, so the placeholder says so
               rather than promising a name search that would return nothing. *@
            <input id="ds-customer" type="search" class="ops-input" placeholder="Card code"
                   @bind="filterCardCode" @bind:after="ApplyFilters" />
        </div>

        <div class="ops-field">
            <label class="ops-label" for="ds-status">Consolidation</label>
            <NocturneSelect Id="ds-status" Class="nsel-block" TValue="string"
                            Options="ConsolidationFilterOptions" @bind-Value="filterStatus"
                            OnChanged="ApplyFilters" Caption="Filter by consolidation"
                            AriaLabel="Filter by consolidation" Placeholder="Any status" />
        </div>

        @* Not a <label>: the segment is three buttons, and a label would
           hand every click to the first of them. *@
        <div class="ops-field ops-ds-seg-field">
            <span class="ops-label" id="ds-period-label">Period</span>
            <div class="ops-ds-seg" role="group" aria-labelledby="ds-period-label">
                <button type="button" class="ops-ds-seg-opt @(period == PeriodToday ? "is-on" : "")"
                        aria-pressed="@(period == PeriodToday)" @onclick="() => SetPeriod(PeriodToday)">Today</button>
                <button type="button" class="ops-ds-seg-opt @(period == PeriodWeek ? "is-on" : "")"
                        aria-pressed="@(period == PeriodWeek)" @onclick="() => SetPeriod(PeriodWeek)">Last 7 days</button>
                <button type="button" class="ops-ds-seg-opt @(period == PeriodCustom ? "is-on" : "")"
                        aria-pressed="@(period == PeriodCustom)" @onclick="() => SetPeriod(PeriodCustom)">Range</button>
            </div>
        </div>

        @if (period == PeriodCustom)
        {
            @* Not <label>s either: NocturneDateField carries a button and a
               popup, which a label would swallow the clicks of. *@
            <div class="ops-ds-dates">
                <div class="ops-field">
                    <span class="ops-label">From</span>
                    <NocturneDateField Id="ds-f-from" Date="filterFromDate" DateChanged="OnFromDateChanged"
                                       AriaLabel="From date" />
                </div>
                <div class="ops-field">
                    <span class="ops-label">To</span>
                    <NocturneDateField Id="ds-f-to" Date="filterToDate" DateChanged="OnToDateChanged"
                                       AriaLabel="To date" />
                </div>
            </div>
        }

        @* The count sits with the controls that decide it rather than under
           the table: it is the answer to the filter row, and by the foot of a
           50-row page the question is off screen. Clear appears only once
           there is something to clear — the design draws it always, but a
           button that does nothing on an unfiltered page is a dead control. *@
        <div class="ops-ds-filter-tail">
            <span class="ops-ds-shown">@shownText</span>
            @if (hasFilters)
            {
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost ops-btn-sm" @onclick="ClearFilters">
                    <i class="ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>Clear
                </button>
            }
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ops-rule-fade"></div>

    @if (isLoading)
    {
        <div class="ops-loading">
            <span class="ops-spin ops-spin-lg"></span>
            <p>Loading desktop sales&hellip;</p>
        </div>
    }
    else if (sales.Count > 0)
    {
        <div>
            <div class="ops-scroll">
                <table class="ops-table mobile-card-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th class="ops-ds-pick">
                                @* Selects the postable rows on this page, not every row that
                                   matches the filters. The button it feeds names a count, and a
                                   count that included rows the operator cannot see would be the
                                   one number on the page they could not check. *@
                                @if (postableOnPage.Count > 0)
                                {
                                    <input type="checkbox" aria-label="Select every postable sale on this page"
                                           title="Select every postable sale on this page"
                                           checked="@allPostableSelected" @onchange="ToggleSelectAll" />
                                }
                            </th>
                            <th>Fiscal number</th>
                            <th>Customer</th>
                            <th>Warehouse</th>
                            <th>Fiscalized</th>
                            <th class="ops-num">Total</th>
                            <th class="ops-num">Paid</th>
                            <th>Payment</th>
                            <th>Fiscal</th>
                            <th>Consolidation</th>
                            @* Empty on purpose: the mark below is a hover cue
                               for a row that already opens the drawer, not a
                               column of data. *@
                            <th class="ops-ds-chev-cell"><span class="visually-hidden">Open</span></th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        @foreach (var sale in sales)
                        {
                            <tr @onclick="() => SelectSale(sale)"
                                class="@RowClass(sale)">
                                @* The cell stops the click rather than the input: a press anywhere
                                   in the gutter should tick the box, and letting either reach the
                                   row would open the drawer over the list being selected. *@
                                <td class="ops-ds-pick" data-label="Select"
                                    @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                                    @if (sale.CanPostToSap)
                                    {
                                        <input type="checkbox" aria-label="@($"Select sale {sale.ExternalReferenceId} for posting")"
                                               checked="@selected.Contains(sale.ExternalReferenceId)"
                                               @onchange="e => ToggleSelected(sale, e)" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        @* Not an empty cell: a row with no box needs to say why, or
                                           it reads as a rendering fault. *@
                                        <span class="ops-ds-nopick" title="@sale.PostRefusal" aria-label="@sale.PostRefusal">
                                            <i class="ph ph-minus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                        </span>
                                    }
                                </td>
                                <td data-label="Fiscal number">
                                    <span class="ops-code">@sale.ExternalReferenceId</span>
                                    @if (sale.SapDocNum.HasValue)
                                    {
                                        <div class="ops-sub">SAP #@sale.SapDocNum</div>
                                    }
                                    else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sale.LastPostingError))
                                    {
                                        <div class="ops-sub ops-ds-rejected" title="@sale.LastPostingError">
                                            SAP refused it@(sale.PostingAttempts > 0 ? $" · {sale.PostingAttempts} attempts" : "")
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                </td>
                                <td data-label="Customer" class="ops-name">
                                    @(sale.CardName ?? sale.CardCode)
                                    @if (sale.CardName != null)
                                    {
                                        <span class="ops-sub"> · @sale.CardCode</span>
                                    }
                                </td>
                                <td data-label="Warehouse">@sale.WarehouseCode</td>
                                <td data-label="Fiscalized" class="ops-ds-when">@Stamp(sale.CreatedAt)</td>
                                <td data-label="Total" class="ops-num">@Money(sale.TotalAmount, sale.Currency)</td>
                                <td data-label="Paid" class="ops-num">@Money(sale.AmountPaid, sale.Currency)</td>
                                @* How it was paid, with the wallet confirmation or slip number under
                                   it — the reference is what an EcoCash sale is reconciled by, so it
                                   belongs on the row rather than only in the drawer. *@
                                <td data-label="Payment">
                                    @TenderName(sale.PaymentMethod)
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sale.PaymentReference))
                                    {
                                        <div class="ops-sub">@sale.PaymentReference</div>
                                    }
                                </td>
                                <td data-label="Fiscal">
                                    <span class="ops-ds-state @FiscalFamily(sale.FiscalizationStatus)">
                                        <span class="ops-dot"></span>@Blank(sale.FiscalizationStatus)
                                    </span>
                                </td>
                                <td data-label="Consolidation">
                                    <span class="ops-ds-state @ConsolidationFamily(sale.ConsolidationStatus)">
                                        <span class="ops-dot"></span>@ConsolidationLabel(sale.ConsolidationStatus)
                                    </span>
                                    @if (sale.ConsolidationId.HasValue)
                                    {
                                        <div class="ops-sub">Run #@sale.ConsolidationId</div>
                                    }
                                </td>
                                <td class="ops-ds-chev-cell">
                                    <i class="ph ph-arrow-right ops-ds-chev" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <div class="ops-ds-foot">
                <span class="ops-ds-foot-info">@footerText</span>
                @if (totalPages > 1)
                {
                    <div class="ops-pages">
                        <button type="button" class="ops-step" disabled="@(currentPage == 1)" @onclick="PreviousPage">
                            <i class="ph ph-caret-left" aria-hidden="true"></i>Previous
                        </button>
                        <span class="ops-page-now">@currentPage of @totalPages</span>
                        <button type="button" class="ops-step" disabled="@(!hasMore)" @onclick="NextPage">
                            Next<i class="ph ph-caret-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="ops-empty">
            <i class="ph ph-receipt" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <h3>@emptyTitle</h3>
            <p>@emptyBody</p>
            @if (hasFilters)
            {
                <div class="ops-empty-actions">
                    <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" @onclick="ClearFilters">
                        <i class="ph ph-x-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>Clear filters
                    </button>
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    }
</div>

@* Both overlays are siblings of `.ops`, not children — see operations.css's
   header for why they carry `.ops-overlay` themselves. *@
@if (showConsolidate)
{
    <div class="ops-overlay ops-overlay-center" @onclick="CloseConsolidate">
        <div class="ops-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Consolidate the day"
             @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
            <div class="ops-dialog-head">
                <h2>Consolidate the day</h2>
                <button type="button" class="ops-x" aria-label="Close" @onclick="CloseConsolidate">
                    <i class="ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
            </div>

            <div class="ops-dialog-body">
                <p class="ops-ds-lede">
                    Everything still awaiting close is uploaded to the back office as one
                    consolidation document. Fiscal numbers stay as they were issued on the device.
                </p>

                <dl class="ops-ds-facts">
                    <dt>Awaiting close</dt>
                    <dd>@(report?.UnpostedInvoiceCount ?? 0)</dd>
                    <dt>Value listed</dt>
                    <dd>@Money(awaitingValue)</dd>
                    <dt>Already consolidated</dt>
                    <dd>@(report?.PostedInvoiceCount ?? 0)</dd>
                    <dt>Posting date</dt>
                    <dd>@DateTime.Today.ToString("dd.MM.yyyy")</dd>
                </dl>

                @if (report != null && report.ReportDate.Date != DateTime.Today)
                {
                    <div class="ops-msg ops-fam-warn">
                        <i class="ph ph-warning" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <div class="ops-msg-body">
                            The figures above are for @report.ReportDate.ToString("dd MMM yyyy"), but the
                            run itself always closes today. Set the period back to Today to see what it
                            will actually pick up.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
            </div>

            <div class="ops-dialog-foot">
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" @onclick="CloseConsolidate">Cancel</button>
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-primary" @onclick="TriggerConsolidation"
                        disabled="@isConsolidating">
                    @if (isConsolidating)
                    {
                        <span class="ops-spin"></span>
                        <span>Consolidating&hellip;</span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <span>Consolidate</span>
                    }
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@if (selectedSale != null)
{
    var fiscalQrImageSrc = FiscalQrCode.ToImageSource(selectedSale.FiscalQRCode);

    <div class="ops-overlay ops-overlay-right" @onclick="CloseDrawer">
        <aside class="ops-drawer ops-ds-drawer" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
               aria-label="Fiscalized invoice @selectedSale.ExternalReferenceId"
               @onclick:stopPropagation="true">

            @* The head states the document rather than the page: a kicker, the
               fiscal reference in full, and the two statuses as marks. The
               reference is a long device-issued string, so it wraps instead of
               being truncated into something nobody can match to a receipt. *@
            <div class="ops-drawer-head ops-ds-dhead">
                <div class="ops-ds-dhead-id">
                    <span class="ops-kicker">Fiscalized invoice</span>
                    <span class="ops-ds-dhead-ref">@selectedSale.ExternalReferenceId</span>
                </div>

                @* Up and down walk the page that is loaded, not the whole
                   result set — paging is what the pager is for, and a Next
                   that silently fetched the next page would move the list
                   under the user while they were reading one row of it. *@
                <div class="ops-ds-dnav">
                    <button type="button" class="ops-icon-btn" title="Previous sale"
                            aria-label="Previous sale" disabled="@(sales.Count < 2)"
                            @onclick="() => StepSale(-1)">
                        <i class="ph ph-caret-up" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="ops-icon-btn" title="Next sale"
                            aria-label="Next sale" disabled="@(sales.Count < 2)"
                            @onclick="() => StepSale(1)">
                        <i class="ph ph-caret-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="ops-icon-btn" title="Close"
                            aria-label="Close" @onclick="CloseDrawer">
                        <i class="ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="ops-ds-dtags">
                    <span class="ops-badge @ConsolidationFamily(selectedSale.ConsolidationStatus)">
                        @ConsolidationLabel(selectedSale.ConsolidationStatus)
                    </span>
                    <span class="ops-ds-state @FiscalFamily(selectedSale.FiscalizationStatus)">
                        <span class="ops-dot"></span>Fiscal @Blank(selectedSale.FiscalizationStatus)
                    </span>
                    @* One timestamp, stated once. The design shows a raised
                       time and a fiscalized time; a desktop sale carries
                       CreatedAt and nothing else, and two labels over one
                       value would invent a gap nobody measured. *@
                    <span class="ops-ds-dwhen">@Full(selectedSale.CreatedAt)</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ops-drawer-body">
                <div class="ops-ds-headline">
                    <b>@Money(selectedSale.TotalAmount, selectedSale.Currency)</b>
                    <span>@tenderText</span>
                </div>

                @* SAP's own words about why it refused, verbatim. Shown whenever there is one and
                   no invoice, which is exactly when somebody has opened this drawer to find out
                   what to do — an operator cannot fix "posting failed". It sits above the facts
                   rather than in the trail below them: the trail states which step a sale stopped
                   at, and a paragraph of SAP table names inside a timeline is unreadable. *@
                @if (!selectedSale.SapDocNum.HasValue && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedSale.LastPostingError))
                {
                    <div class="ops-msg ops-fam-bad" role="alert">
                        <i class="ph ph-warning-octagon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <div class="ops-msg-body">
                            <strong>SAP has not accepted this sale.</strong>
                            <div class="ops-ds-sapsaid">@selectedSale.LastPostingError</div>
                            @if (selectedSale.PostingAttempts > 0)
                            {
                                <div class="ops-sub">
                                    @selectedSale.PostingAttempts attempt@(selectedSale.PostingAttempts == 1 ? "" : "s") so far.
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }

                <div class="ops-defs">
                    <div>
                        <div class="ops-def-k">Customer</div>
                        <div class="ops-def-v">@(selectedSale.CardName ?? selectedSale.CardCode)</div>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="ops-def-k">Card code</div>
                        <div class="ops-def-v">@selectedSale.CardCode</div>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="ops-def-k">Warehouse</div>
                        <div class="ops-def-v">@selectedSale.WarehouseCode</div>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="ops-def-k">Raised in</div>
                        <div class="ops-def-v">@Blank(selectedSale.SourceSystem)</div>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="ops-def-k">Captured by</div>
                        <div class="ops-def-v">@Blank(selectedSale.CreatedBy)</div>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="ops-def-k">Payment method</div>
                        <div class="ops-def-v">@Blank(selectedSale.PaymentMethod)</div>
                    </div>
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedSale.PaymentReference))
                    {
                        <div>
                            <div class="ops-def-k">Payment reference</div>
                            <div class="ops-def-v">@selectedSale.PaymentReference</div>
                        </div>
                    }
                    @* What this sale became in SAP, as a fact rather than only as a line in the
                       trail — it is the number somebody opens this drawer to copy, and a timeline
                       entry is not where you go to copy a number.

                       Two routes reach SAP and they write different columns, so both are stated
                       and neither is left to be inferred from the other's absence. A blank SAP
                       invoice on a consolidated sale does not mean it never got there; it means
                       the run's invoice carries it, which is what the sub-line says. *@
                    @if (selectedSale.SapDocNum.HasValue)
                    {
                        <div>
                            <div class="ops-def-k">SAP invoice</div>
                            <div class="ops-def-v">#@selectedSale.SapDocNum</div>
                        </div>
                    }
                    @if (selectedSale.ConsolidationId.HasValue)
                    {
                        <div>
                            <div class="ops-def-k">Consolidation run</div>
                            <div class="ops-def-v">
                                #@selectedSale.ConsolidationId
                                @if (!selectedSale.SapDocNum.HasValue)
                                {
                                    <div class="ops-sub">carries the SAP invoice for this sale</div>
                                }
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    }
                    @if (selectedSale.PostedAt.HasValue)
                    {
                        <div>
                            <div class="ops-def-k">Posted</div>
                            <div class="ops-def-v">@Full(selectedSale.PostedAt.Value)</div>
                        </div>
                    }
                    @* Stated only once the invoice exists. Before that "not attempted" is not news
                       — there is nothing for a payment to settle. *@
                    @if (selectedSale.SapDocNum.HasValue)
                    {
                        <div>
                            <div class="ops-def-k">Settlement</div>
                            <div class="ops-def-v">
                                <span class="ops-ds-state @PaymentFamily(selectedSale.PaymentStatus)">
                                    <span class="ops-dot"></span>@PaymentLabel(selectedSale.PaymentStatus)
                                </span>
                                @if (selectedSale.PaymentSapDocNum.HasValue)
                                {
                                    <div class="ops-sub">Payment #@selectedSale.PaymentSapDocNum</div>
                                }
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>

                @if (selectedSale.Lines.Count > 0)
                {
                    <div class="ops-ds-block">
                        <div class="ops-def-k">Lines</div>
                        <table class="ops-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Item</th>
                                    <th class="ops-num">Qty</th>
                                    <th class="ops-num">Unit price</th>
                                    <th class="ops-num">Total</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (var line in selectedSale.Lines)
                                {
                                    <tr>
                                        <td>
                                            <span class="ops-code">@line.ItemCode</span>
                                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(line.ItemDescription))
                                            {
                                                <div class="ops-sub">@line.ItemDescription</div>
                                            }
                                        </td>
                                        <td class="ops-num">@QuantityDisplay.Format(line.Quantity)</td>
                                        <td class="ops-num">@line.UnitPrice.ToString("N2")</td>
                                        <td class="ops-num">@line.LineTotal.ToString("N2")</td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                            </tbody>
                        </table>

                        @* Just "VAT": the design labels it 13%, but the rate is
                           charged per line at its own tax code's rate — see
                           CreateDesktopSaleHandler — so a basket carrying a
                           zero-rated item is not 13% of anything. *@
                        <div class="ops-ds-sum">
                            <div>
                                <span>Net</span>
                                <span>@Money(selectedSale.TotalAmount - selectedSale.VatAmount, selectedSale.Currency)</span>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <span>VAT</span>
                                <span>@Money(selectedSale.VatAmount, selectedSale.Currency)</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="ops-ds-sum-total">
                                <span>Total</span>
                                <span>@Money(selectedSale.TotalAmount, selectedSale.Currency)</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }

                @* The receipt the device issued, which lives on the sale and nowhere else: it was
                   signed under this external reference rather than a SAP document number, so the
                   invoice this sale becomes carries no QR to fall back on.

                   This is where the design's "fiscal signature" panel landed. The design draws the
                   signature as a line of text; the code is a URL, so it is drawn as the scannable
                   thing it is and the text beside it carries what a phone call needs — the
                   verification code in the blocks of four the receipt prints, and the same URL as
                   a link for anyone reading this at a desk. *@
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(fiscalQrImageSrc))
                {
                    <div class="ops-ds-qr">
                        <div class="ops-ds-qr-plate">
                            <img src="@fiscalQrImageSrc" alt="ZIMRA fiscal receipt QR code" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="ops-ds-qr-copy">
                            <div class="ops-def-k">Fiscal signature</div>
                            <div class="ops-ds-qr-title">Scan to verify this fiscal receipt</div>
                            <p>
                                Issued on the device for @selectedSale.ExternalReferenceId@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedSale.FiscalDeviceNumber)
                                    ? "" : $" · device {selectedSale.FiscalDeviceNumber}")@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedSale.FiscalDayNo)
                                    ? "" : $" · fiscal day {selectedSale.FiscalDayNo}").
                            </p>
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedSale.FiscalVerificationCode))
                            {
                                <div class="ops-ds-qr-code">
                                    <span class="ops-def-k">Verification code</span>
                                    @* Grouped in fours, the way the receipt prints it and the way
                                       FiscalReceiptQrComposer.FormatVerificationCode renders it on
                                       the API side. Display only — ZIMRA is sent it unbroken. *@
                                    <span class="ops-code">@GroupCode(selectedSale.FiscalVerificationCode)</span>
                                </div>
                            }
                            @if (verifyUrl != null)
                            {
                                <div class="ops-ds-qr-code">
                                    <a class="ops-ds-verify" href="@verifyUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                                        Verify with ZIMRA<i class="ph ph-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </a>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }

                <div class="ops-ds-block">
                    <div class="ops-def-k">Consolidation trail</div>
                    <div class="ops-ds-trail">
                        @foreach (var step in trail)
                        {
                            <div class="ops-ds-trail-step @step.Family">
                                <div class="ops-ds-trail-rail">
                                    <span class="ops-ds-trail-mark @(step.IsNow ? "is-now" : "")"></span>
                                </div>
                                <div class="ops-ds-trail-body">
                                    <div class="ops-ds-trail-label">@step.Label</div>
                                    <div class="ops-ds-trail-meta">@step.Meta</div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            @* The design draws "Consolidate now", "Exclude from close" and "Receipt PDF" here.
               Post to SAP is not any of the three, and is deliberately not labelled as if it
               were: posting sends this one sale to SAP as its own invoice, which is what
               `POST sales/{reference}/post` does, while consolidating is the end-of-day run that
               folds a whole day into one invoice per customer. There is still no endpoint that
               excludes a sale from the close, and no receipt PDF is kept for one. *@
            <div class="ops-drawer-foot">
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" @onclick="CloseDrawer">Close</button>
                @if (string.Equals(selectedSale.FiscalizationStatus, "Success", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                {
                    <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-primary" @onclick="OpenDesktopCredit">
                        <i class="ph ph-arrow-u-up-left" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        Credit notes
                    </button>
                }
                @if (selectedSale.CanPostToSap)
                {
                    <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-primary"
                            @onclick="() => PostOne(selectedSale)"
                            disabled="@(isPosting || isLoading)">
                        @if (postingReference == selectedSale.ExternalReferenceId)
                        {
                            <span class="ops-spin"></span>
                            <span>Posting&hellip;</span>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <i class="ph ph-cloud-arrow-up" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span>Post to SAP</span>
                        }
                    </button>
                }
                else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedSale.PostRefusal))
                {
                    @* The reason stands in the button's place rather than a disabled button
                       standing there greyed out with nothing to explain it. *@
                    <span class="ops-ds-foot-why">@selectedSale.PostRefusal</span>
                }
            </div>
        </aside>
    </div>
}

@* Confirmed before it runs, like the consolidation is, and for a stronger reason: a SAP invoice
   cannot be withdrawn, only reversed by a credit note. The dialog states the count and the value
   about to reach SAP, because those are the two numbers somebody would want to have checked. *@
@if (showBulkPost)
{
    <div class="ops-overlay ops-overlay-center" @onclick="CloseBulkPost">
        <div class="ops-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Post sales to SAP"
             @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
            <div class="ops-dialog-head">
                <h2>Post @selected.Count to SAP</h2>
                <button type="button" class="ops-x" aria-label="Close" @onclick="CloseBulkPost">
                    <i class="ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
            </div>

            <div class="ops-dialog-body">
                <p class="ops-ds-lede">
                    Each of these becomes one A/R invoice in SAP, keeping its own fiscal receipt.
                    They are sent one at a time; a sale SAP refuses does not stop the rest.
                </p>

                <dl class="ops-ds-facts">
                    <dt>Sales selected</dt>
                    <dd>@selected.Count</dd>
                    <dt>Value selected</dt>
                    <dd>@Money(selectedValue)</dd>
                    <dt>Posting date</dt>
                    <dd>@DateTime.Today.ToString("dd.MM.yyyy")</dd>
                </dl>

                <div class="ops-msg ops-fam-info">
                    <i class="ph ph-shield-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="ops-msg-body">
                        Sending this twice is safe. Each sale is claimed before anything reaches SAP,
                        so a sale that has already posted is reported with the invoice it became
                        rather than being invoiced again.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ops-dialog-foot">
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" @onclick="CloseBulkPost">Cancel</button>
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-primary" @onclick="PostSelected"
                        disabled="@isPosting">
                    @if (isPosting)
                    {
                        <span class="ops-spin"></span>
                        <span>Posting&hellip;</span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <span>Post @selected.Count to SAP</span>
                    }
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@* What the batch actually did, sale by sale. A summary line alone would not do: the whole point of
   posting a set is that its members can end differently, and "4 of 5 posted" names neither the one
   that did not nor why. *@
@if (bulkResult != null)
{
    <div class="ops-overlay ops-overlay-center" @onclick="CloseBulkResult">
        <div class="ops-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Posting results"
             @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
            <div class="ops-dialog-head">
                <h2>@bulkResult.InSap of @bulkResult.Requested in SAP</h2>
                <button type="button" class="ops-x" aria-label="Close" @onclick="CloseBulkResult">
                    <i class="ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
            </div>

            <div class="ops-dialog-body">
                <div class="ops-scroll">
                    <table class="ops-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Sale</th>
                                <th>Outcome</th>
                                <th>Detail</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var row in bulkResult.Results)
                            {
                                <tr>
                                    <td><span class="ops-code">@row.ExternalReferenceId</span></td>
                                    <td>
                                        <span class="ops-ds-state @PostOutcomeFamily(row.Outcome)">
                                            <span class="ops-dot"></span>@PostOutcomeLabel(row.Outcome)
                                        </span>
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="ops-name">
                                        @if (row.SapDocNum.HasValue)
                                        {
                                            <span>Invoice #@row.SapDocNum</span>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            @Blank(row.Message)
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="ops-dialog-foot">
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-primary" @onclick="CloseBulkResult">Done</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@if (creditSale != null)
{
    <div class="ops-overlay ops-overlay-center">
        <div class="ops-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="desktop-credit-title"
             style="width:min(960px,95vw);max-height:90vh;overflow:auto">
            <div class="ops-dialog-head">
                <h2 id="desktop-credit-title">Credit notes · @creditSale.ExternalReferenceId</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="ops-dialog-body">
                <p>Create a fiscal credit against the original REVMax receipt, including before SAP posting.
                    The SAP credit memo and the stock return follow on their own: at once if this sale is
                    already in SAP, otherwise as soon as it posts.</p>
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(desktopCreditError))
                {
                    <p role="alert">@desktopCreditError</p>
                }
                @if (desktopCreditBusy)
                {
                    <p role="status"><span class="ops-spin"></span> Reading or submitting the saved credit note…</p>
                }
                @foreach (var note in desktopCreditNotes)
                {
                    <div class="ops-ds-card" style="margin-bottom:12px">
                        <strong>@note.Number · @Money(note.Amount, note.Currency)</strong>
                        @* Both halves, in words. "Deferred" is the API's word for a correct, ordinary
                           state — the sale simply has not posted yet — and showing it raw would read
                           to an operator as something having gone wrong. *@
                        <p>Fiscal: @note.Status · SAP: @DesktopCreditSapLabel(note)</p>
                        <p>@note.Reason</p>
                        <p>@note.Message</p>
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(note.SapError))
                        {
                            <p role="alert">@note.SapError</p>
                        }
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(note.ReceiptGlobalNo))
                        {
                            <p>Credit receipt: @note.ReceiptGlobalNo</p>
                        }
                        @if (FiscalQrCode.ToImageSource(note.QrCode) is { Length: > 0 } qr)
                        {
                            <img src="@qr" alt="Credit note verification QR code" width="160" height="160" />
                        }
                        @if (note.Status is "Submitting" or "ReconciliationRequired" or "Prepared")
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" disabled="@desktopCreditBusy"
                                    @onclick="() => CheckDesktopCredit(note)">@(note.Status == "Prepared" ? "Continue fiscalisation" : "Check fiscal status")</button>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
                @if (desktopCreditForm != null && !desktopCreditSubmitted)
                {
                    <p>Original receipt: @desktopCreditForm.Source.ReceiptGlobalNo · Device @desktopCreditForm.Source.DeviceId ·
                        Fiscal day @desktopCreditForm.Source.FiscalDayNo</p>
                    <div class="ops-scroll">
                        <table class="ops-table">
                            <thead><tr><th>Receipt line</th><th>Available</th><th>Credit quantity</th><th>Credit amount</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (var line in desktopCreditLines)
                                {
                                    <tr>
                                        <td>@line.Source.Name</td><td>@line.Available</td>
                                        <td><input type="number" class="ops-input" aria-label="Credit quantity for @line.Source.Name"
                                                   min="0" max="@line.Available" step="0.000001" @bind="line.Quantity" disabled="@desktopCreditBusy" /></td>
                                        <td>@Money(decimal.Round(line.Quantity * line.Source.UnitPrice, 2, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero), desktopCreditForm.Source.Currency)</td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <label class="ops-label" for="desktop-credit-reason">Reason for credit</label>
                    <textarea id="desktop-credit-reason" class="ops-input" maxlength="500" @bind="desktopCreditReason"
                              disabled="@desktopCreditBusy"></textarea>
                    <p>Total credit: <strong>@Money(DesktopCreditAmount, desktopCreditForm.Source.Currency)</strong></p>
                }
            </div>
            <div class="ops-dialog-foot">
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" disabled="@desktopCreditBusy" @onclick="() => creditSale = null">Close</button>
                <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-ghost" disabled="@desktopCreditBusy" @onclick="RefreshDesktopCredits">Refresh</button>
                @if (desktopCreditForm != null && !desktopCreditSubmitted)
                {
                    <button type="button" class="ops-btn ops-btn-primary" disabled="@(!CanCreateDesktopCredit)"
                            @onclick="CreateDesktopCredit">Create and fiscalise with REVMax</button>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    private DesktopSaleDto? creditSale;
    private DesktopCreditForm? desktopCreditForm;
    private List<DesktopCreditNoteResult> desktopCreditNotes = [];
    private List<DesktopCreditSelection> desktopCreditLines = [];
    private bool desktopCreditBusy;
    private bool desktopCreditSubmitted;
    private string? desktopCreditError;
    private string desktopCreditReason = "";
    private string desktopCreditKey = "";
    private decimal DesktopCreditAmount => desktopCreditLines.Sum(l => decimal.Round(l.Quantity * l.Source.UnitPrice, 2, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero));
    private bool CanCreateDesktopCredit => !desktopCreditBusy && !desktopCreditSubmitted &&
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(desktopCreditReason) && desktopCreditLines.Any(l => l.Quantity > 0) &&
        desktopCreditLines.All(l => l.Quantity >= 0 && l.Quantity <= l.Available);
    private sealed class DesktopCreditSelection(DesktopCreditLine source, decimal available)
    {
        public DesktopCreditLine Source { get; } = source;
        public decimal Available { get; } = Math.Max(0, available);
        public decimal Quantity { get; set; }
    }

    private async Task OpenDesktopCredit()
    {
        creditSale = selectedSale;
        selectedSale = null;
        desktopCreditNotes = [];
        await RefreshDesktopCredits();
    }

    private async Task RefreshDesktopCredits()
    {
        if (creditSale == null || desktopCreditBusy) return;
        desktopCreditBusy = true;
        desktopCreditForm = null;
        desktopCreditError = null;
        try
        {
            // Load saved results even when REVMax is unavailable or the original cannot be prepared.
            desktopCreditNotes = await DesktopService.GetCreditNotesAsync(creditSale.ExternalReferenceId);
            desktopCreditForm = await DesktopService.PrepareCreditNoteAsync(creditSale.ExternalReferenceId);
            desktopCreditLines = desktopCreditForm.Source.Lines.Select(l => new DesktopCreditSelection(l,
                l.Quantity - desktopCreditForm.ReservedQuantities.GetValueOrDefault(l.LineNo))).ToList();
            desktopCreditKey = Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
            desktopCreditReason = "";
            desktopCreditSubmitted = false;
        }
        catch (Exception ex) { desktopCreditError = ex.Message; }
        finally { desktopCreditBusy = false; }
    }

    private async Task CreateDesktopCredit()
    {
        if (creditSale == null || !CanCreateDesktopCredit) return;
        desktopCreditBusy = true;
        desktopCreditSubmitted = true;
        desktopCreditError = null;
        try
        {
            var result = await DesktopService.CreateCreditNoteAsync(creditSale.ExternalReferenceId,
                new CreateDesktopCreditRequest(desktopCreditKey, desktopCreditReason,
                    desktopCreditLines.Where(l => l.Quantity > 0).Select(l => new DesktopCreditQuantity(l.Source.LineNo, l.Quantity)).ToList()));
            desktopCreditNotes.Insert(0, result);
        }
        catch (Exception ex) { desktopCreditError = ex.Message + " Refresh to check the saved notes before creating another credit."; }
        finally { desktopCreditBusy = false; }
    }

    private async Task CheckDesktopCredit(DesktopCreditNoteResult note)
    {
        if (creditSale == null || desktopCreditBusy) return;
        desktopCreditBusy = true;
        try
        {
            var result = note.Status == "Prepared"
                ? await DesktopService.ContinueCreditNoteAsync(creditSale.ExternalReferenceId, note.Id)
                : await DesktopService.ReconcileCreditNoteAsync(creditSale.ExternalReferenceId, note.Id);
            var index = desktopCreditNotes.FindIndex(n => n.Id == note.Id);
            if (index >= 0) desktopCreditNotes[index] = result;
        }
        catch (Exception ex) { desktopCreditError = ex.Message; }
        finally { desktopCreditBusy = false; }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Where the back-office half of a credit stands, said in words rather than by status name.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The SAP memo is raised on its own — at once when the sale is already in SAP, otherwise when it
    /// posts — so most of these describe something happening rather than something owed. The two that
    /// do not (a refusal, and a consolidated sale) are the ones an operator has to act on.
    /// </remarks>
    private static string DesktopCreditSapLabel(DesktopCreditNoteResult note) => note.SapDocNum.HasValue
        ? $"credit memo #{note.SapDocNum}"
        : note.SapStatus switch
        {
            DesktopCreditSapStatuses.Deferred => "follows once this sale posts",
            DesktopCreditSapStatuses.NotRequired => "nothing owed — this sale is not posted to SAP",
            DesktopCreditSapStatuses.ManualInSap => "raise by hand against the consolidated invoice",
            DesktopCreditSapStatuses.Failed => "failed — will be retried",
            // A status this build predates. Shown rather than swallowed.
            _ => note.SapStatus
        };

    private const string PeriodToday = "today";
    private const string PeriodWeek = "week";
    private const string PeriodCustom = "custom";

    private List<DesktopSaleDto> sales = new();
    private List<WarehouseDto> warehouses = new();

    private IEnumerable<NocturneSelectOption<string>> WarehouseFilterOptions =>
        warehouses
            .Where(w => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(w.WarehouseCode))
            .Select(w => new NocturneSelectOption<string>(w.WarehouseCode!, w.WarehouseCode!, "info"))
            .Prepend(NocturneSelectOption.All("All warehouses"));

    private static readonly NocturneSelectOption<string>[] ConsolidationFilterOptions =
    [
        new(string.Empty, "Any status", "neutral") { IsUnset = true, RuleAfter = true },
        new("Pending", "Awaiting close", "warn"),
        new("Consolidated", "Consolidated", "good"),
        new("Failed", "Failed", "bad"),
        new("Excluded", "Excluded", "neutral")
    ];
    private DesktopSaleDto? selectedSale;
    private EndOfDayReportDto? report;

    private bool isLoading;
    private bool isConsolidating;
    private bool isExporting;
    private bool showConsolidate;
    private DateTime? lastPolledAt;

    // ── Posting to SAP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Selection is held by external reference rather than by row index or by the DTO itself: a
    // SignalR push reloads this page underneath the operator, and after it every `DesktopSaleDto`
    // in `sales` is a different object. Keyed on the reference, a selection survives that reload —
    // and the reference is what the API is sent anyway.

    private readonly HashSet<string> selected = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    private bool isPosting;

    /// <summary>The one sale a single post is in flight for, so only its button spins.</summary>
    private string? postingReference;

    private bool showBulkPost;
    private DesktopSalesBulkPostResultDto? bulkResult;

    private List<DesktopSaleDto> postableOnPage => sales.Where(s => s.CanPostToSap).ToList();

    private bool allPostableSelected =>
        postableOnPage.Count > 0 && postableOnPage.All(s => selected.Contains(s.ExternalReferenceId));

    private decimal selectedValue =>
        sales.Where(s => selected.Contains(s.ExternalReferenceId)).Sum(s => s.TotalAmount);

    // One notice for everything this page does itself; the Snackbar is left to
    // the push events, which arrive while the user is looking elsewhere.
    private string? notice;
    private string noticeFamily = "ops-fam-info";
    private string noticeIcon = "ph-info";

    // Filters
    private string filterWarehouse = "";
    private string filterCardCode = "";
    private string filterStatus = "";
    private string period = PeriodToday;
    private DateTime? filterFromDate;
    private DateTime? filterToDate;

    // Pagination
    private int currentPage = 1;
    private int pageSize = 50;
    private int totalCount;
    private bool hasMore;
    private int totalPages => totalCount > 0 ? (int)Math.Ceiling((double)totalCount / pageSize) : 1;

    private bool hasFilters =>
        filterWarehouse != "" || filterCardCode != "" || filterStatus != "" || period != PeriodToday;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        filterFromDate = DateTime.Today;
        filterToDate = DateTime.Today;

        var warehouseList = await MasterDataCache.GetWarehousesAsync();
        warehouses = warehouseList?.Where(w => w.IsActive).ToList() ?? new();

        await LoadData();
        await AuditService.LogAsync(AuditActions.ViewDesktopTransactions, "DesktopSale", null);

        HubService.OnDesktopSaleCreated += OnSaleCreated;
        HubService.OnConsolidationCompleted += OnConsolidationDone;
    }

    private async void OnSaleCreated()
    {
        await InvokeAsync(async () =>
        {
            Snackbar.Add("New desktop sale received", Severity.Info);
            await LoadData();
            StateHasChanged();
        });
    }

    private async void OnConsolidationDone()
    {
        await InvokeAsync(async () =>
        {
            Snackbar.Add("Consolidation completed — data refreshed", Severity.Success);
            await LoadData();
            StateHasChanged();
        });
    }

    // ── Loading ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadData()
    {
        isLoading = true;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            var response = await DesktopService.GetDesktopSalesAsync(
                string.IsNullOrEmpty(filterWarehouse) ? null : filterWarehouse,
                string.IsNullOrEmpty(filterCardCode) ? null : filterCardCode,
                string.IsNullOrEmpty(filterStatus) ? null : filterStatus,
                filterFromDate,
                filterToDate,
                currentPage,
                pageSize);

            if (response != null)
            {
                sales = response.Sales;
                totalCount = response.TotalCount;
                hasMore = response.HasMore;
                lastPolledAt = DateTime.Now;

                // After every reload, including the ones a SignalR push triggers. A sale that has
                // just posted is no longer postable, so this is also what takes it back out of the
                // selection when somebody else posted it while this page was open.
                PruneSelection();

                ClearError();
            }
            else
            {
                SayError("Failed to load desktop sales. Check that the API is running.");
            }

            report = await DesktopService.GetEndOfDayReportAsync(filterFromDate);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            SayError($"Error: {ex.Message}");
        }
        finally
        {
            isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    private async Task RefreshData()
    {
        currentPage = 1;
        await LoadData();
    }

    // ── Filters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Every one of these is a single deliberate act — picking a warehouse,
    // committing a card code, choosing a period — so each reloads on its own
    // rather than waiting behind a Search button the design does not draw.

    private async Task ApplyFilters()
    {
        currentPage = 1;
        await LoadData();
    }

    private async Task SetPeriod(string value)
    {
        if (period == value)
        {
            return;
        }

        period = value;

        if (value == PeriodToday)
        {
            filterFromDate = DateTime.Today;
            filterToDate = DateTime.Today;
        }
        else if (value == PeriodWeek)
        {
            filterFromDate = DateTime.Today.AddDays(-6);
            filterToDate = DateTime.Today;
        }
        // "custom" keeps whatever pair is already in the fields and reveals them.

        await ApplyFilters();
    }

    private async Task OnFromDateChanged(DateTime? value)
    {
        filterFromDate = value;
        await ApplyFilters();
    }

    private async Task OnToDateChanged(DateTime? value)
    {
        filterToDate = value;
        await ApplyFilters();
    }

    private async Task ClearFilters()
    {
        filterWarehouse = "";
        filterCardCode = "";
        filterStatus = "";
        period = PeriodToday;
        filterFromDate = DateTime.Today;
        filterToDate = DateTime.Today;
        await ApplyFilters();
    }

    // ── Paging ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task NextPage()
    {
        if (hasMore)
        {
            currentPage++;
            await LoadData();
        }
    }

    private async Task PreviousPage()
    {
        if (currentPage > 1)
        {
            currentPage--;
            await LoadData();
        }
    }

    // ── The detail drawer ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void SelectSale(DesktopSaleDto sale) => selectedSale = sale;

    private void CloseDrawer() => selectedSale = null;

    // Picked and open are different states and a row can be both: picked is
    // what the Post button will send, open is what the drawer is showing.
    private string RowClass(DesktopSaleDto sale)
    {
        var picked = selected.Contains(sale.ExternalReferenceId);
        var open = selectedSale?.Id == sale.Id;
        return picked && open ? "is-picked is-open" : picked ? "is-picked" : open ? "is-open" : "";
    }

    // Up and down wrap within the loaded page. Falling off the end into the
    // next page would fetch behind the drawer and rewrite the list underneath
    // it; the pager is where changing page belongs.
    private void StepSale(int direction)
    {
        if (selectedSale == null || sales.Count < 2)
        {
            return;
        }

        var index = sales.FindIndex(s => s.Id == selectedSale.Id);
        if (index < 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        selectedSale = sales[((index + direction) % sales.Count + sales.Count) % sales.Count];
    }

    // What the customer handed over, and what went back. A sale can carry no
    // tender at all — an account transfer the till never settled, a card that
    // was declined — and "tendered 0.00 · change 0.00" states that far less
    // clearly than saying so.
    private string tenderText
    {
        get
        {
            var sale = selectedSale!;
            if (sale.AmountPaid <= 0)
            {
                return "no payment recorded";
            }

            var tendered = $"tendered {Money(sale.AmountPaid, sale.Currency)}";
            var change = sale.AmountPaid - sale.TotalAmount;
            return change > 0 ? $"{tendered} · change {Money(change, sale.Currency)}" : tendered;
        }
    }

    // The QR payload is the ZIMRA verification URL, not an image — see
    // FiscalReceiptQrComposer.BuildQrPayload, which composes it as
    // {qrUrl}/{device}{date}{receipt}{code}. FiscalQrCode.ToImageSource renders
    // it as something scannable; this is the same string as something clickable,
    // for whoever is reading the drawer at a desk rather than holding a phone.
    // Anything that is not an http(s) URL gets no link: the column is 500
    // characters of whatever the platform returned, and older rows predate the
    // composer.
    private string? verifyUrl
    {
        get
        {
            var raw = selectedSale?.FiscalQRCode?.Trim();
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(raw))
            {
                return null;
            }

            return Uri.TryCreate(raw, UriKind.Absolute, out var uri) &&
                   (uri.Scheme == Uri.UriSchemeHttp || uri.Scheme == Uri.UriSchemeHttps)
                ? raw
                : null;
        }
    }

    // Blocks of four, the way the receipt prints it and the way the API's
    // FiscalReceiptQrComposer.FormatVerificationCode renders it. Display only —
    // the code goes to ZIMRA unbroken, and nothing here sends it anywhere.
    private static string GroupCode(string? code)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(code))
        {
            return "";
        }

        var groups = new List<string>();
        for (var i = 0; i < code.Length; i += 4)
        {
            groups.Add(code.Substring(i, Math.Min(4, code.Length - i)));
        }

        return string.Join("-", groups);
    }

    // ── The trail ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Four steps, each read off a column rather than a script: when the sale
    // was captured, whether the device signed it, whether the close took it,
    // and what it became in SAP. The design's fourth step assumes a ledger
    // posting time this page has no field for; the SAP document number is the
    // fact that actually answers "and then what", so that is what it states.
    //
    // The last step is the one place the trail and the drawer's refusal banner
    // describe the same thing. They are not redundant: the banner carries SAP's
    // verbatim words, which is a paragraph, and the trail says which step the
    // sale stopped at, which is a line.

    private sealed record TrailStep(string Label, string Meta, string Family, bool IsNow = false);

    private List<TrailStep> trail
    {
        get
        {
            var sale = selectedSale!;

            var origin = new List<string> { Full(sale.CreatedAt) };
            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sale.CreatedBy))
            {
                origin.Add(sale.CreatedBy);
            }
            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sale.SourceSystem))
            {
                origin.Add(sale.SourceSystem);
            }

            var steps = new List<TrailStep>
            {
                new("Raised in the desktop app", string.Join(" · ", origin), "ops-fam-good")
            };

            steps.Add(sale.FiscalizationStatus?.ToLowerInvariant() switch
            {
                "success" => new TrailStep(
                    "Fiscalized on the device",
                    string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sale.FiscalReceiptNumber)
                        ? "the authority accepted the receipt"
                        : $"receipt {sale.FiscalReceiptNumber} accepted",
                    "ops-fam-good"),
                "failed" => new TrailStep(
                    "Fiscalization failed",
                    "the device could not sign this receipt",
                    "ops-fam-bad"),
                "skipped" => new TrailStep(
                    "Fiscalization skipped",
                    "this sale was not put to the device",
                    "ops-fam-neutral"),
                _ => new TrailStep(
                    "Awaiting fiscalization",
                    "the device has not signed this receipt yet",
                    "ops-fam-accent",
                    IsNow: true)
            });

            steps.Add(sale.ConsolidationStatus?.ToLowerInvariant() switch
            {
                "consolidated" => new TrailStep(
                    "Consolidated into the back office",
                    sale.ConsolidationId.HasValue ? $"run #{sale.ConsolidationId}" : "closed",
                    "ops-fam-good"),
                "failed" => new TrailStep(
                    "Consolidation failed",
                    "the run could not take this sale",
                    "ops-fam-bad"),
                "excluded" => new TrailStep(
                    "Excluded from the close",
                    "left out of the consolidation run",
                    "ops-fam-neutral"),
                _ => new TrailStep(
                    "Awaiting day close",
                    "stays on the device until the day is consolidated",
                    "ops-fam-accent",
                    IsNow: true)
            });

            // Two routes reach SAP and they write different columns. The
            // per-sale posting job — and the Post to SAP button, which is the
            // same work asked for now — stamps SapDocNum on the row; the
            // end-of-day run groups a customer's sales into one consolidated
            // invoice and stamps the DocNum on the *consolidation*, leaving only
            // ConsolidationId here. Reading one and not the other is why a
            // consolidated sale used to look like it had gone nowhere.
            if (sale.SapDocNum.HasValue)
            {
                var meta = sale.PostedAt.HasValue
                    ? $"invoice {sale.SapDocNum} · {Full(sale.PostedAt.Value)}"
                    : $"invoice {sale.SapDocNum}";
                steps.Add(new TrailStep("Posted to SAP", meta, "ops-fam-good"));
            }
            else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sale.LastPostingError))
            {
                steps.Add(new TrailStep(
                    "SAP refused it",
                    sale.PostingAttempts > 0
                        ? $"{sale.PostingAttempts} attempt{(sale.PostingAttempts == 1 ? "" : "s")} so far — see above for what SAP said"
                        : "see above for what SAP said",
                    "ops-fam-bad"));
            }
            else if (sale.ConsolidationId.HasValue)
            {
                steps.Add(new TrailStep(
                    "Posted with the consolidation run",
                    $"run #{sale.ConsolidationId} carries the SAP invoice, not this row",
                    "ops-fam-good"));
            }
            else if (Is(sale.ConsolidationStatus, "Consolidated"))
            {
                steps.Add(new TrailStep(
                    "No SAP document recorded",
                    "the sale is closed, but nothing on this row names the invoice it became",
                    "ops-fam-warn"));
            }
            else if (Is(sale.ConsolidationStatus, "Excluded"))
            {
                steps.Add(new TrailStep(
                    "No SAP document",
                    "an excluded sale is never invoiced",
                    "ops-fam-neutral"));
            }
            else
            {
                steps.Add(new TrailStep(
                    "Not in SAP yet",
                    sale.CanPostToSap
                        ? "posts with the day, or now with Post to SAP"
                        : "posts as part of the day's consolidation",
                    "ops-fam-neutral"));
            }

            return steps;
        }
    }

    // ── Posting to SAP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void ToggleSelected(DesktopSaleDto sale, ChangeEventArgs args)
    {
        if (args.Value is true)
        {
            selected.Add(sale.ExternalReferenceId);
        }
        else
        {
            selected.Remove(sale.ExternalReferenceId);
        }
    }

    /// <remarks>
    /// Clears only this page's postable rows rather than the whole set, so unticking here does not
    /// silently drop a selection made on a page the operator has already left.
    /// </remarks>
    private void ToggleSelectAll(ChangeEventArgs args)
    {
        var references = postableOnPage.Select(s => s.ExternalReferenceId);

        if (args.Value is true)
        {
            foreach (var reference in references)
            {
                selected.Add(reference);
            }
        }
        else
        {
            foreach (var reference in references.ToList())
            {
                selected.Remove(reference);
            }
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Drops references the current list no longer offers.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Called after every reload. Without it a filter change would leave a selection the operator
    /// cannot see, and the hero would offer to post rows that are no longer on the page — which is
    /// the one thing a count on a button must never do.
    /// </remarks>
    private void PruneSelection()
    {
        if (selected.Count == 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        var onPage = sales
            .Where(s => s.CanPostToSap)
            .Select(s => s.ExternalReferenceId)
            .ToHashSet(StringComparer.Ordinal);

        selected.RemoveWhere(reference => !onPage.Contains(reference));
    }

    private void OpenBulkPost() => showBulkPost = true;

    private void CloseBulkPost() => showBulkPost = false;

    private void CloseBulkResult() => bulkResult = null;

    /// <summary>
    /// Posts the one sale open in the drawer.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The drawer closes on success and stays open on failure. A sale that posted has nothing left
    /// to say — the row behind it now carries its invoice number — while a sale SAP refused is
    /// exactly what the drawer is for, and closing it would hide the reason the operator asked for.
    /// </remarks>
    private async Task PostOne(DesktopSaleDto sale)
    {
        if (isPosting)
        {
            return;
        }

        isPosting = true;
        postingReference = sale.ExternalReferenceId;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            var (result, error) = await DesktopService.PostSaleToSapAsync(sale.ExternalReferenceId);

            if (error is not null)
            {
                SayError(error);
                await LoadData();
                return;
            }

            selected.Remove(sale.ExternalReferenceId);
            selectedSale = null;

            Say(
                result!.Message ?? $"{sale.ExternalReferenceId} reached SAP.",
                result.Outcome == DesktopSalePostOutcomes.Posted ? "ops-fam-good" : "ops-fam-info",
                result.Outcome == DesktopSalePostOutcomes.Posted ? "ph-check-circle" : "ph-info");

            await LoadData();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            SayError($"The post could not be sent: {ex.Message}");
        }
        finally
        {
            isPosting = false;
            postingReference = null;
        }
    }

    private async Task PostSelected()
    {
        if (isPosting || selected.Count == 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        isPosting = true;
        StateHasChanged();

        // Snapshotted before the call. A push can reload `sales` while this is in flight, and the
        // results have to be matched against what was actually sent.
        var references = selected.ToList();

        try
        {
            var (result, error) = await DesktopService.PostSalesToSapAsync(references);
            showBulkPost = false;

            if (error is not null)
            {
                SayError(error);
                await LoadData();
                return;
            }

            bulkResult = result;

            // Only the ones SAP now holds leave the selection. Whatever failed or was refused stays
            // ticked, so pressing the button again retries exactly those rather than making the
            // operator find them in the list a second time.
            foreach (var row in result!.Results.Where(InSap))
            {
                selected.Remove(row.ExternalReferenceId);
            }

            Say(Summarise(result), SummaryFamily(result), SummaryIcon(result));
            await LoadData();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            showBulkPost = false;
            SayError($"The batch could not be completed: {ex.Message}");
            await LoadData();
        }
        finally
        {
            isPosting = false;
        }
    }

    private static bool InSap(DesktopSalePostResultDto row) =>
        row.Outcome is DesktopSalePostOutcomes.Posted or DesktopSalePostOutcomes.AlreadyInSap;

    private static string Summarise(DesktopSalesBulkPostResultDto result)
    {
        var parts = new List<string>();

        if (result.Posted > 0) parts.Add($"{result.Posted} posted");
        if (result.AlreadyInSap > 0) parts.Add($"{result.AlreadyInSap} already in SAP");
        if (result.InProgress > 0) parts.Add($"{result.InProgress} already being posted");
        if (result.Failed > 0) parts.Add($"{result.Failed} refused by SAP");
        if (result.NotPostable > 0) parts.Add($"{result.NotPostable} not postable");

        return parts.Count == 0
            ? "Nothing was posted."
            : $"{string.Join(", ", parts)}.";
    }

    // A batch with anything unresolved in it is not a success, whatever else went right: the row
    // that did not post is the one somebody has to come back to.
    private static string SummaryFamily(DesktopSalesBulkPostResultDto result) =>
        result.Failed > 0 ? "ops-fam-bad"
        : result.NotPostable > 0 || result.InProgress > 0 ? "ops-fam-warn"
        : "ops-fam-good";

    private static string SummaryIcon(DesktopSalesBulkPostResultDto result) =>
        result.Failed > 0 ? "ph-warning-octagon"
        : result.NotPostable > 0 || result.InProgress > 0 ? "ph-warning"
        : "ph-check-circle";

    // ── Consolidation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void OpenConsolidate() => showConsolidate = true;

    private void CloseConsolidate() => showConsolidate = false;

    private decimal awaitingValue => report?.UnpostedSales.Sum(s => s.Amount) ?? 0m;

    private async Task TriggerConsolidation()
    {
        isConsolidating = true;
        StateHasChanged();
        try
        {
            var success = await DesktopService.TriggerConsolidationAsync();
            showConsolidate = false;

            if (success)
            {
                Say("End-of-day consolidation triggered. The back office picks the invoices up as the run completes.",
                    "ops-fam-good", "ph-check-circle");
                await LoadData();
            }
            else
            {
                SayError("The consolidation run could not be started.");
            }
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            showConsolidate = false;
            SayError($"Consolidation failed: {ex.Message}");
        }
        finally
        {
            isConsolidating = false;
        }
    }

    private async Task ExportToExcel()
    {
        if (sales.Count == 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        isExporting = true;
        StateHasChanged();
        try
        {
            var bytes = ExportService.ExportDesktopSalesToExcel(sales, report, filterFromDate, filterToDate);
            var base64 = Convert.ToBase64String(bytes);
            await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("downloadFile", $"Desktop_Sales_{DateTime.Now:yyyyMMdd_HHmm}.xlsx", base64);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            SayError($"Export failed: {ex.Message}");
        }
        finally
        {
            isExporting = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    // ── Notices ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void Say(string text, string family, string icon)
    {
        notice = text;
        noticeFamily = family;
        noticeIcon = icon;
    }

    private void SayError(string text) => Say(text, "ops-fam-bad", "ph-warning-octagon");

    // A successful reload clears a failure that is no longer true, and leaves a
    // consolidation result standing — that one is news, not an error state.
    private void ClearError()
    {
        if (noticeFamily == "ops-fam-bad")
        {
            notice = null;
        }
    }

    // ── The day summary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private sealed record Lane(string Name, int Count, string Family);

    private string dayLabel => report == null
        ? "Day in progress"
        : report.ReportDate.Date == DateTime.Today
            ? "Day in progress"
            : report.ReportDate.ToString("dd MMM yyyy");

    // Drawn from the report rather than from `sales`, which is one page of a
    // filtered list and would make the lanes disagree with the total above them.
    // The unposted list carries a status per row; the counts it does not explain
    // fall into "awaiting close", so the four always add up to the day.
    private List<Lane> lanes
    {
        get
        {
            if (report == null)
            {
                return new();
            }

            var listed = report.UnpostedSales;
            var failed = listed.Count(s => Is(s.ConsolidationStatus, "Failed"));
            var excluded = listed.Count(s => Is(s.ConsolidationStatus, "Excluded"));
            var awaiting = Math.Max(0, report.UnpostedInvoiceCount - failed - excluded);

            return new()
            {
                new Lane("Awaiting close", awaiting, "ops-fam-accent"),
                new Lane("Consolidated", report.PostedInvoiceCount, "ops-fam-good"),
                new Lane("Failed", failed, "ops-fam-bad"),
                new Lane("Excluded", excluded, "ops-fam-neutral")
            };
        }
    }

    private int laneTotal => lanes.Sum(l => l.Count);

    private List<BPSummaryDto> topPartners => report?.BusinessPartnerSummaries
        .Where(b => b.TotalAmount > 0)
        .OrderByDescending(b => b.TotalAmount)
        .Take(5)
        .ToList() ?? new();

    private decimal topPartnerMax => topPartners.Count > 0 ? topPartners.Max(b => b.TotalAmount) : 0m;

    // ── Text ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    // The count answers the filter row and sits with it; the foot is left to
    // say how fresh the rows under it are. The design puts a "refreshes every
    // 30s" note there — nothing on this page polls on a timer, so it says what
    // actually brings a new row in.
    private string shownText => $"Showing {sales.Count} of {totalCount} · newest first";

    private string footerText => lastPolledAt.HasValue
        ? $"Polled {lastPolledAt:HH:mm:ss} · rows arrive as the devices report in"
        : "Rows arrive as the devices report in";

    private string emptyTitle => hasFilters ? "Nothing matches these filters" : "The day is clear";

    private string emptyBody => hasFilters
        ? "Widen the period or clear the filters to see the rest of the day."
        : "Invoices fiscalized on the desktop apps appear here within a few seconds of being issued.";

    // ── Formatting ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    // The report carries no currency of its own, so its figures borrow the one
    // the loaded sales are in. With nothing loaded the amount stands alone
    // rather than being labelled with a guess.
    private string currencyCode => sales.FirstOrDefault()?.Currency ?? "";

    private string Money(decimal value) => Money(value, currencyCode);

    private static string Money(decimal value, string? code) =>
        string.IsNullOrEmpty(code) ? value.ToString("N2") : $"{code} {value.ToString("N2")}";

    private static string Percent(int part, int whole) =>
        whole <= 0 ? "0%" : ((double)part / whole * 100).ToString("0.##", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + "%";

    private static string Percent(decimal part, decimal whole) =>
        whole <= 0 ? "0%" : ((double)(part / whole) * 100).ToString("0.##", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + "%";

    // The +2h is the app's standing display offset for these timestamps.
    private static string Stamp(DateTime createdAt)
    {
        var local = createdAt.AddHours(2);
        return local.Date == DateTime.Today ? local.ToString("HH:mm") : local.ToString("dd MMM HH:mm");
    }

    // The drawer states a date whatever day the row is from: it is read on its
    // own, away from the column that made "12:17" unambiguous.
    private static string Full(DateTime utc) => utc.AddHours(2).ToString("dd MMM yyyy, HH:mm");

    private static bool Is(string? status, string value) =>
        string.Equals(status, value, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    private static string Blank(string? text) => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(text) ? "—" : text;

    // A tender as the counter names it. Older rows carry the till's own casing, so the comparison is
    // case-blind; a sale nobody recorded a tender for says so rather than showing an empty cell.
    private static string TenderName(string? tender) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(tender) ? "Not recorded"
        : tender.Trim().Equals("ecocash", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) ? "EcoCash"
        : tender.Trim();

    private static string ConsolidationLabel(string? status) =>
        Is(status, "Pending") ? "Awaiting close" : Blank(status);

    private static string FiscalFamily(string? status) => status?.ToLowerInvariant() switch
    {
        "success" => "ops-fam-good",
        "pending" => "ops-fam-warn",
        "failed" => "ops-fam-bad",
        "skipped" => "ops-fam-neutral",
        _ => "ops-fam-neutral"
    };

    // Awaiting close takes the accent rather than a warning hue: it is the
    // expected state of a sale the day has not closed on yet, not a problem.
    private static string ConsolidationFamily(string? status) => status?.ToLowerInvariant() switch
    {
        "consolidated" => "ops-fam-good",
        "pending" => "ops-fam-accent",
        "failed" => "ops-fam-bad",
        "excluded" => "ops-fam-neutral",
        _ => "ops-fam-neutral"
    };

    // A settlement that was never attempted is not a fault — most of these are read seconds after
    // the invoice posted — so null takes the accent the way "awaiting close" does. Unmapped is a
    // warning rather than a failure: nothing broke, but no amount of waiting will fix it either.
    private static string PaymentFamily(string? status) => status switch
    {
        DesktopSalePaymentStatuses.Posted => "ops-fam-good",
        DesktopSalePaymentStatuses.PostedUnconfirmed => "ops-fam-good",
        DesktopSalePaymentStatuses.Failed => "ops-fam-bad",
        DesktopSalePaymentStatuses.Unmapped => "ops-fam-warn",
        _ => "ops-fam-accent"
    };

    private static string PaymentLabel(string? status) => status switch
    {
        DesktopSalePaymentStatuses.Posted => "Settled",
        // Named for what actually happened rather than for the status word. SAP showed the invoice
        // already paid, so nothing was sent — and an operator reading "PostedUnconfirmed" would
        // reasonably go looking for a payment this system never made.
        DesktopSalePaymentStatuses.PostedUnconfirmed => "Already settled in SAP",
        DesktopSalePaymentStatuses.Failed => "Payment failed",
        DesktopSalePaymentStatuses.Unmapped => "Tender not mapped",
        _ => "Not settled yet"
    };

    private static string PostOutcomeFamily(string? outcome) => outcome switch
    {
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.Posted => "ops-fam-good",
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.AlreadyInSap => "ops-fam-good",
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.InProgress => "ops-fam-accent",
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.Failed => "ops-fam-bad",
        _ => "ops-fam-warn"
    };

    private static string PostOutcomeLabel(string? outcome) => outcome switch
    {
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.Posted => "Posted",
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.AlreadyInSap => "Already in SAP",
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.InProgress => "Being posted",
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.Failed => "SAP refused it",
        DesktopSalePostOutcomes.NotPostable => "Not postable",
        _ => Blank(outcome)
    };

    public void Dispose()
    {
        HubService.OnDesktopSaleCreated -= OnSaleCreated;
        HubService.OnConsolidationCompleted -= OnConsolidationDone;
    }
}
